  "instructions": [
    "Heat the olive oil in a large deep skillet or pot over medium heat. Add the garlic and cook for 30 seconds until fragrant but not browned.",
    "Add the penne, water, salt, and oregano. Bring to a boil over high heat.",
    "Reduce to a steady simmer and cook for 9 to 11 minutes, stirring often, until the pasta is tender and most of the water is absorbed.",
    "Stir in the frozen peas and cook for 2 minutes until hot and bright green.",
    "Add the tuna, capers, lemon zest, and lemon juice. Break the tuna into small flakes as you stir.",
    "Cook for 1 to 2 minutes until the tuna is warm. Add a splash of water if the pasta looks dry.",
    "Season with the black pepper and stir in the parsley. Serve hot."
